  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Project STARS (Space Travel And Research Strategy)


    First proposed
    in 2035, and officially beginning in 2046, project STARS was humanity''s most
    ambitious attempt to explore the universe. Divided into four different phases,
    it carefully laid foundations, defined requirements, detailed steps, and set
    realistic objectives needed to reach planets far beyond our solar system.


    Phase
    one required a monumental technological jump, as every renowned scientist around
    the world gathered to figure out the fastest and most efficient way to travel
    through space. Simultaneously, mass industrialization was set in motion to prepare
    the production of soon-to-be-needed satellites, starships, space platforms, and
    more.


    After years of progress and unparalleled breakthroughs, phase two
    began in 2062, when the first unmanned mission to test faster-than-light travel
    was initiated. Many failures followed, as humanity adapted, improved, and eventually
    overcame the complex task of traveling quickly and safely.


    The year 2086
    marks the start of phase three: the first expedition with a crew set to visit
    and analyze several solar systems where life could be sustainable. The most advanced
    spacecraft to date, Pinta IV, currently carries 20 volunteers towards every promising
    star, where they will scan planets in hopes of finding suitable conditions for
    human survival.


    We find ourselves waiting for news, while we continue to
    prepare for the glorious day in which we move into phase four: the large scale
    migration to a new world.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
